  {
   "id": 631870,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<p>The expressions <span data-math=\"s(60 − 12s)\">s(60 − 12s)</span> and <span data-math=\"-12s^2 + 60s\">-12s^2 + 60s</span> define the same function. A soap bubble machine can launch many soap bubbles into the air before they begin to pop. The function given models the number of soap bubbles floating in the air in <span data-math=\"s\">s</span> seconds.</p>\n<p>According to the function, how many seconds have passed before all of the bubbles have been made and also popped?</p>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1223090,
     "content_html": "7 seconds"
    },
    {
     "id": 1223089,
     "content_html": "6 seconds"
    },
    {
     "id": 1223091,
     "content_html": "5 seconds"
    },
    {
     "id": 1223088,
     "content_html": "0 seconds"
    }
